35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found out that road closures didn't stop community halls from working! But the scanning suppliers seem really unreliable with their timing.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interesting. It seems our past attempts at digitisation were a failure, whereas community-led groups have shown remarkable resilience over six years.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"We have plenty of skilled volunteers for tools, but absolutely no one on staff who can actually supervise them or certify the equipment.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The funding is the problem. Grants only cover the first year of sessions, and last year's vehicle costs were way over budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The bus links are gone in two wards. People have to travel an hour now just to reach a library counter. It's really unfair.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that's terrible! We have to do something for those people. But @Minako, if the vehicle costs are too high, is a mobile service possible?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"The data suggests that ""top-down"" projects like digitisation fail, while ""bottom-up"" partner programs thrive. We should favor the latter.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"If we go with a workshop, we're in trouble. We have the tools and the volunteers, but no one to legally oversee them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Exactly. A mobile service would likely bleed the budget dry by year two, given the running costs and the grant structure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,But if we don't go to them... they just can't use the library at all.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,What about the language circles? They sound like the kind of partner-run groups Benjamin mentioned!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. They align with the historical success of unaided partner groups and avoid the pitfalls of expensive equipment or unreliable contractors.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"As long as they are coordinated by partner organizations and not dumped on our untrained staff, it's the most logical choice.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"From a budget perspective, if the partners carry the weight after the first year, it's the only sustainable option.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Would those circles be in the outer wards? If they are, it helps the people who lost their buses.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I really hope so! It feels like the kind of thing that would bring people together without breaking.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It avoids the ""room-sound"" trap. It's a proven model of community resilience rather than a flashy new gadget.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I'm satisfied with that, provided the facilitators are external. It keeps the staff workload manageable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. It's the most fiscally responsible and sustainable path forward.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,If it reaches the outer wards... then I'm okay with it too.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
